1
00:00:03,128 --> 00:00:04,296
How's your mom holding up?

2
00:00:04,505 --> 00:00:07,382
She's doing okay,
but we just lost another nurse.

3
00:00:07,591 --> 00:00:08,634
How many is that now?

4
00:00:08,842 --> 00:00:12,346
Two, and I know what you're
thinking: she's eating them.

5
00:00:14,723 --> 00:00:16,850
She's just so impossible,
they keep quitting.

6
00:00:17,059 --> 00:00:18,477
So, who's watching her now?

7
00:00:18,685 --> 00:00:22,064
A bowl full of M&amp;M's
with a few Ambien tossed in.

8
00:00:22,648 --> 00:00:23,690
What up, guys?

9
00:00:23,899 --> 00:00:24,942
-Hello.
-Hey.

10
00:00:26,068 --> 00:00:28,403
Okay, well, now that everyone's here,

11
00:00:28,612 --> 00:00:30,906
Penny and I have some big news.

12
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:32,783
We're engaged!

13
00:00:32,991 --> 00:00:35,869
Oh, my God! Congratulations!

14
00:00:39,122 --> 00:00:41,542
And I thought me having sex with
Emily was gonna be the big news.

15
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:43,210
(ALL CHEERING)

16
00:00:44,836 --> 00:00:46,964
-Oh, my God!
-Hey! Hey!

17
00:00:48,465 --> 00:00:50,342
What the hell!

18
00:00:51,218 --> 00:00:54,429
You guys propose all the time.
This never happens.

19
00:00:55,389 --> 00:00:56,807
You're right!

20
00:00:58,725 --> 00:01:01,311
(THEME SONG PLAYS)

21
00:01:23,542 --> 00:01:25,502
Boy, I'm so hungry today.

22
00:01:26,545 --> 00:01:28,130
I wonder why?

23
00:01:29,965 --> 00:01:31,717
Because you had sex the other night?

24
00:01:32,801 --> 00:01:34,344
You know what?

25
00:01:34,553 --> 00:01:36,305
That may be it.

26
00:01:37,973 --> 00:01:39,933
By the way,
it isn't like riding a bike.

27
00:01:40,142 --> 00:01:41,977
Like, I fell off a few times.

28
00:01:44,938 --> 00:01:47,106
-Hey, buddy.
-Hello.

29
00:01:47,316 --> 00:01:48,483
You okay?

30
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:52,571
I just got called
into President Siebert's office.

31
00:01:53,655 --> 00:01:55,616
The university
won't let me switch my field

32
00:01:55,824 --> 00:01:58,327
of study to inflationary
cosmology.

33
00:01:58,535 --> 00:02:01,121
They're forcing me
to continue with string theory.

34
00:02:01,330 --> 00:02:04,291
-Why?
-He said it's why they hired me,

35
00:02:04,541 --> 00:02:06,460
it's what my grant
was designated for,

36
00:02:06,668 --> 00:02:10,047
and that everybody has to
do things they don't want to do.

37
00:02:10,255 --> 00:02:12,132
He then gave an example
of something he had to do,

38
00:02:12,341 --> 00:02:15,260
even though he didn't want to,
which was look at my stupid face.

39
00:02:17,596 --> 00:02:20,974
That's a rude thing to say out loud.

40
00:02:23,393 --> 00:02:26,980
It's an outrage. Honestly, I'm
tempted to leave the university.

41
00:02:27,189 --> 00:02:29,149
You know, if you're
really serious about that,

42
00:02:29,358 --> 00:02:31,652
I hear there are some
exciting opportunities

43
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:34,071
in home care for the old and fat.

44
00:02:35,656 --> 00:02:38,325
Whatever you do,
just don't make any rash decisions.

45
00:02:38,533 --> 00:02:41,203
I don't know. I am really aggravated.

46
00:02:42,371 --> 00:02:44,831
When I'm feeling low,
I have sex with a girl.

47
00:02:46,875 --> 00:02:48,585
But that's just me.

48
00:02:52,005 --> 00:02:53,715
-Oh, come on, give her a chance.
-No.

49
00:02:53,924 --> 00:02:56,175
No, life, it is too short.

50
00:02:58,011 --> 00:02:59,763
I know you've only been here
a day and a half,

51
00:02:59,971 --> 00:03:01,848
but you're like part of the family!

52
00:03:04,183 --> 00:03:07,020
I don't think the service
is gonna send any more people.

53
00:03:07,229 --> 00:03:12,191
Yeah, maybe it's time we just
release Ma back into the sea.

54
00:03:14,695 --> 00:03:15,737
That's not helpful.

55
00:03:15,946 --> 00:03:18,824
Well, then, we may need
to get used to the idea

56
00:03:19,032 --> 00:03:22,160
that we're gonna be living here
the next few months.

57
00:03:22,369 --> 00:03:25,580
But we have jobs.
We can't babysit her 24 hours a day.

58
00:03:25,789 --> 00:03:28,500
Well, what if we use
our vacation time?

59
00:03:28,709 --> 00:03:32,379
I wanted to go to Hawaii, not Hell.

60
00:03:32,587 --> 00:03:34,464
I don't know what else we can do.

61
00:03:35,507 --> 00:03:39,845
Howie, I love you, and as your wife,
your mother is every bit

62
00:03:40,053 --> 00:03:43,140
as much my problem
as she is yours, so...

63
00:03:44,433 --> 00:03:46,560
...I want a divorce.

64
00:03:50,397 --> 00:03:51,440
Hello, Leonard.

65
00:03:51,648 --> 00:03:52,983
Hi, Mom.

66
00:03:53,191 --> 00:03:54,943
I have some exciting news.

67
00:03:55,152 --> 00:03:57,821
I'm listening.

68
00:03:58,655 --> 00:04:00,824
Before I tell you,
will you promise to try

69
00:04:01,032 --> 00:04:04,578
and be happy for me and keep
any concerns you have to yourself?

70
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:06,663
No.

71
00:04:08,915 --> 00:04:12,251
Let me save you all
of your hemming and hawing.

72
00:04:12,461 --> 00:04:15,464
Sheldon already told me
that you and Penny are engaged.

73
00:04:17,174 --> 00:04:19,760
I hate that you talk to him
more than you talk to me.

74
00:04:19,968 --> 00:04:22,304
Would you like for you
and me to talk more?

75
00:04:24,848 --> 00:04:27,267
You know what? It's probably fine.

76
00:04:27,476 --> 00:04:30,645
In any event,
while I've had my misgivings

77
00:04:30,854 --> 00:04:32,981
about... Penny...

78
00:04:34,566 --> 00:04:36,568
...Sheldon spoke very fondly of her,

79
00:04:36,777 --> 00:04:38,570
and if she is good enough for him,

80
00:04:38,779 --> 00:04:40,822
then she's good enough for me.

81
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:47,078
I'm your son. What about the fact
that she's good enough for me?

82
00:04:49,164 --> 00:04:50,707
Sure.

83
00:04:52,209 --> 00:04:53,251
Thanks, Mom.

84
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:55,294
Leonard, would it make
you feel better

85
00:04:55,504 --> 00:04:59,591
to hear that your mother
approved of your life choices?

86
00:05:01,384 --> 00:05:02,552
Yes, it would.

87
00:05:02,761 --> 00:05:06,097
Yeah, well, you should work on that.

88
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:14,439
No, Mom, it's the same guy I've gone
out with for the past two years.

89
00:05:14,648 --> 00:05:16,650
Yeah, the scientist.

90
00:05:16,858 --> 00:05:21,238
Well, it's complicated. I mean, he
works with lasers and atomic magnets.

91
00:05:25,158 --> 00:05:26,993
No, I did not see it coming.

92
00:05:27,202 --> 00:05:30,330
No, we did not set a date.
No, I'm not pregnant.

93
00:05:31,957 --> 00:05:34,209
Yeah, this is a first for our family.

94
00:05:35,085 --> 00:05:37,712
All right, tell Dad I love him.
I gotta go. All right, bye.

95
00:05:37,921 --> 00:05:41,216
-Atomic magnets?
-Shut up.

96
00:05:42,592 --> 00:05:44,094
Sorry I'm late.
The leaf blower broke,

97
00:05:44,302 --> 00:05:46,847
so I had to hand-dry
my mother-in-law.

98
00:05:47,055 --> 00:05:48,098
(DOOR CLOSES)

99
00:05:48,306 --> 00:05:50,517
-You want some wine?
-Thanks.

100
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:53,311
Little warning before you jump
into this marriage business:

101
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:55,689
you're not just marrying him,
you're marrying his family.

102
00:05:55,897 --> 00:05:58,024
I think Leonard's mom's okay with me.

103
00:05:58,233 --> 00:06:00,318
It doesn't matter if she's okay
with you. The question is:

104
00:06:00,527 --> 00:06:02,571
can she go
to the bathroom by herself?

105
00:06:08,201 --> 00:06:09,744
Hit me again.

106
00:06:11,538 --> 00:06:13,582
So, what are the living
arrangements gonna be?

107
00:06:13,790 --> 00:06:16,001
Well, haven't really talked
about it yet, but I figure,

108
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:18,503
at some point, I'll move in
with him, or he'll move in with me.

109
00:06:18,712 --> 00:06:21,089
Well, with you not working,
that makes financial sense.

110
00:06:21,298 --> 00:06:25,051
You're not working! How would you
like a job in home health care?

111
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:27,178
Not a chance.

112
00:06:27,386 --> 00:06:28,847
-Please. I'm desperate.
-No.

113
00:06:29,055 --> 00:06:31,141
-I'll pay you anything you want.
-Okay, then, yeah.

114
00:06:33,226 --> 00:06:35,228
No! Keep your money!

115
00:06:39,608 --> 00:06:42,110
I could've ridden
a bull longer than that.

116
00:06:45,572 --> 00:06:47,449
What you working on?

117
00:06:47,657 --> 00:06:49,993
I'm writing an appeal
to the Faculty Senate,

118
00:06:50,201 --> 00:06:52,037
so that I can move
on from string theory.

119
00:06:52,245 --> 00:06:53,496
How's it going?

120
00:06:54,873 --> 00:06:55,916
You tell me.

121
00:06:56,124 --> 00:06:57,292
(CLEARS THROAT)

122
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:59,210
"Dear esteemed colleagues,

123
00:06:59,418 --> 00:07:02,297
As you may know, I have requested
to change my field of study.

124
00:07:02,505 --> 00:07:06,509
My decision to do so is, I believe,
in the best interest of science.

125
00:07:06,718 --> 00:07:09,262
At your convenience,
I'd be happy to explain it to you

126
00:07:09,471 --> 00:07:11,973
in words you'll understand."

127
00:07:14,059 --> 00:07:16,144
It's nice that
you called them esteemed.

128
00:07:17,228 --> 00:07:19,022
You're right. I'll take that out.

129
00:07:20,941 --> 00:07:23,818
So, listen, there was something
I was hoping to float past you.

130
00:07:24,486 --> 00:07:26,071
Now that Penny and I are engaged,

131
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:28,657
I thought we might want to talk
about our living arrangements.

132
00:07:29,699 --> 00:07:30,742
Of course.

133
00:07:30,951 --> 00:07:33,703
She's spent many nights here,
and you're worried

134
00:07:33,912 --> 00:07:37,916
about preserving the myth
of her virginity before the wedding.

135
00:07:41,252 --> 00:07:42,295
-I'm not.
-Good,

136
00:07:42,504 --> 00:07:43,672
because not only
has that ship sailed,

137
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:46,716
if it hit an iceberg,
countless men would perish.

138
00:07:49,052 --> 00:07:51,179
Actually, this is about
where she and I are going to live.

139
00:07:51,388 --> 00:07:52,806
What do you mean?

140
00:07:53,014 --> 00:07:55,809
Well, well, we might
want to live together.

141
00:07:56,017 --> 00:07:59,145
Oh, yeah, well, I've already
given this some thought,

142
00:07:59,354 --> 00:08:03,775
and I'm willing
to let Penny live with us

143
00:08:03,984 --> 00:08:06,403
one day a week for a trial period.

144
00:08:08,363 --> 00:08:11,199
Now, obviously,
not when she's made cranky

145
00:08:11,408 --> 00:08:14,202
by the shedding
of her uterine lining.

146
00:08:16,246 --> 00:08:17,288
That's very sweet.

147
00:08:19,207 --> 00:08:23,545
But we were thinking more of us
maybe living together with...

148
00:08:24,379 --> 00:08:25,422
...not you.

149
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:30,260
I don't understand.

150
00:08:31,845 --> 00:08:34,681
How could we all live together
if I'm not there?

151
00:08:36,683 --> 00:08:38,727
Look, I know this is...
this is change,

152
00:08:38,935 --> 00:08:41,479
-and that sounds scary--
-Where are you going to go?

153
00:08:41,688 --> 00:08:43,314
I don't know.

154
00:08:43,523 --> 00:08:45,483
We just started to think about this.

155
00:08:45,692 --> 00:08:46,901
Maybe I'll move in with Penny,

156
00:08:47,110 --> 00:08:49,904
or maybe she and I'll take this
place, you can move across the hall.

157
00:08:50,113 --> 00:08:52,115
Move across the hall?

158
00:08:53,033 --> 00:08:55,577
Did you take a marijuana?

159
00:08:58,538 --> 00:08:59,998
No, I did not.

160
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:02,709
Did you get hit on the head
with a coconut?

161
00:09:03,877 --> 00:09:05,879
-No.
-Well, then, I'm all out of guesses.

162
00:09:06,087 --> 00:09:09,466
What? Me move across the hall-- Why
would you even suggest such a thing?

163
00:09:09,674 --> 00:09:13,303
Because I love Penny, and want
to give her the life she deserves.

164
00:09:13,928 --> 00:09:15,138
I see.

165
00:09:15,346 --> 00:09:18,475
You're putting your future
bride's happiness above mine.

166
00:09:21,227 --> 00:09:23,271
Well, yeah.

167
00:09:25,148 --> 00:09:26,274
Wow.

168
00:09:31,237 --> 00:09:34,532
How dare the university force me
to go back to string theory!

169
00:09:34,741 --> 00:09:36,367
They just don't appreciate you.

170
00:09:36,576 --> 00:09:38,995
Yeah, and on top of that,
Leonard has the audacity

171
00:09:39,204 --> 00:09:41,372
to suggest that now
that he and Penny are engaged,

172
00:09:41,581 --> 00:09:43,541
he may not want
to live with me anymore.

173
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:45,502
Here, I made you
some Strawberry Quik.

174
00:09:45,710 --> 00:09:47,420
I have real problems here, Amy.

175
00:09:47,629 --> 00:09:50,340
I can't be mollified with
a beverage designed for children.

176
00:09:51,466 --> 00:09:52,967
Mm. Yummy.

177
00:09:55,011 --> 00:09:56,596
You know,
this might work out for the best.

178
00:09:56,805 --> 00:10:00,016
You're always complaining about
what a terrible roommate Leonard is.

179
00:10:00,225 --> 00:10:02,769
Like how he turns up
the thermostat when you're not there.

180
00:10:02,977 --> 00:10:06,272
Ugh. It's like
walking into the Amazon.

181
00:10:06,481 --> 00:10:08,483
And not the good Amazon
with one-day shipping.

182
00:10:08,691 --> 00:10:11,111
The awful one with birds and snakes.

183
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:14,697
You hate the sound of all
those keys on his key chain.

184
00:10:14,906 --> 00:10:16,783
Four keys!

185
00:10:16,991 --> 00:10:19,160
Who does he think he is, a warden?

186
00:10:21,162 --> 00:10:22,831
See? Maybe you'll love living alone.

187
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:25,625
I don't know. Perhaps.

188
00:10:25,834 --> 00:10:30,004
And if it turns out you don't...
you and I could live together.

189
00:10:30,213 --> 00:10:32,382
You and--
Oh, sure.

190
00:10:33,299 --> 00:10:35,385
And while we're at it,
why don't we get engaged, too?

191
00:10:35,593 --> 00:10:37,470
Why don't we get a little house,
start a family?

192
00:10:37,679 --> 00:10:41,141
Enjoy our sunset years together?
Do you hear yourself, woman?

193
00:10:43,101 --> 00:10:45,603
-Sheldon, it was just a thought.
-No. Here's a thought.

194
00:10:45,812 --> 00:10:47,897
You're not moving in,
Leonard's not moving out,

195
00:10:48,106 --> 00:10:50,233
everything stays
exactly the way it is.

196
00:10:50,441 --> 00:10:53,570
And by the way, I saw you make
this Strawberry Quik with syrup,

197
00:10:53,778 --> 00:10:56,406
and you're supposed
to use the powder!

198
00:10:57,031 --> 00:10:59,325
-It tastes the same.
-No. The syrup tastes better,

199
00:10:59,534 --> 00:11:01,035
and I don't like it.

200
00:11:04,414 --> 00:11:07,250
This is so sweet!
You never cook for me.

201
00:11:07,458 --> 00:11:10,253
Well, you cook for me
all the time and...

202
00:11:10,461 --> 00:11:11,629
(GROANS)

203
00:11:12,964 --> 00:11:15,633
If you don't like my cooking,
why haven't you ever said anything?

204
00:11:15,842 --> 00:11:19,220
It's hard to talk
with so much heavy chewing to do.

205
00:11:20,972 --> 00:11:24,017
-Sorry. I'll get better.
-I know you'll try.

206
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:28,605
So, should we talk
about setting a date?

207
00:11:28,813 --> 00:11:31,316
Well, I'd like to pick one that works
with my brother's schedule.

208
00:11:31,524 --> 00:11:33,026
Okay, and when would that be?

209
00:11:33,735 --> 00:11:36,362
Uh, 12 to 18 months from now,
depending on good behavior.

210
00:11:37,238 --> 00:11:38,281
(KNOCKING)

211
00:11:39,324 --> 00:11:41,743
-Hi, is Sheldon here?
-No, I thought he was with you.

212
00:11:41,951 --> 00:11:43,786
He was, but he stormed off.

213
00:11:43,995 --> 00:11:46,080
-Now he isn't answering his phone.
-What happened?

214
00:11:46,289 --> 00:11:48,333
He was really angry
that you suggested he move out.

215
00:11:48,541 --> 00:11:49,751
Oh.

216
00:11:49,959 --> 00:11:51,710
I also mentioned
that he and I could live together,

217
00:11:51,920 --> 00:11:54,589
but he was too mad at you to realize
what a great idea that is.

218
00:11:57,050 --> 00:11:59,010
Well, he's been having
a couple of tough days.

219
00:11:59,219 --> 00:12:00,261
I'm sure he's fine.

220
00:12:00,470 --> 00:12:02,931
He probably just needs
a little alone time to decompress.

221
00:12:03,139 --> 00:12:05,058
You're probably right.

222
00:12:05,266 --> 00:12:07,060
So, what are you guys doing?

223
00:12:09,395 --> 00:12:12,941
Well, Leonard cooked for me and now
we're just having a nice dinner,

224
00:12:13,149 --> 00:12:15,526
you know, as a newly engaged couple.

225
00:12:15,734 --> 00:12:17,195
That's nice.

226
00:12:22,909 --> 00:12:24,743
Anyway, as I was saying,

227
00:12:24,953 --> 00:12:27,664
Sheldon probably just
needs a little alone time.

228
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:31,834
'Cause that's important.

229
00:12:34,295 --> 00:12:36,422
Not just for him, but for...

230
00:12:37,423 --> 00:12:39,259
...most anybody, really.

231
00:12:39,467 --> 00:12:41,552
Don't I know it.

232
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:43,388
-What is that, polenta?
-Amy, get out.

233
00:12:43,638 --> 00:12:44,681
Right.

234
00:12:50,311 --> 00:12:51,354
No.

235
00:12:55,316 --> 00:12:56,359
Hey, Sheldon.

236
00:12:56,567 --> 00:12:58,111
What happened?

237
00:12:58,319 --> 00:13:00,113
I was cooking
in the back room last night

238
00:13:00,321 --> 00:13:04,200
-and the hot plate caught on fire.
-And you couldn't put it out?

239
00:13:04,409 --> 00:13:06,995
I was across the street
at the do-it-yourself car wash,

240
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:08,538
taking a shower.

241
00:13:11,833 --> 00:13:13,334
So when will you reopen?

242
00:13:13,626 --> 00:13:18,131
Um, I don't know. I'm waiting to hear
back from the insurance company.

243
00:13:19,007 --> 00:13:20,717
So, tomorrow?

244
00:13:22,093 --> 00:13:24,012
I don't mean to be rude,
Sheldon, but,

245
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:26,180
my life is kind of
falling apart right now.

246
00:13:26,389 --> 00:13:27,598
Your life?

247
00:13:27,806 --> 00:13:30,310
The university is making me
do string theory,

248
00:13:30,518 --> 00:13:33,896
and my girlfriend loves me
so much she wants to live with me.

249
00:13:35,315 --> 00:13:39,569
And now, the place I need to go when
I'm sad is damp and smells funny.

250
00:13:41,612 --> 00:13:43,406
Well, sorry I let you down.

251
00:13:43,614 --> 00:13:46,200
No, I do not accept this.

252
00:13:46,409 --> 00:13:48,536
Everything is changing and I hate it.

253
00:13:48,745 --> 00:13:51,414
It stops now. I'm helping you
get back on your feet.

254
00:13:53,791 --> 00:13:56,377
I would like to purchase
this comic book, please.

255
00:13:58,421 --> 00:13:59,589
That'll be $2.99.

256
00:13:59,797 --> 00:14:02,383
Really? It's soaking wet.

257
00:14:03,384 --> 00:14:04,427
Fine, a dollar.

258
00:14:07,846 --> 00:14:10,641
-Can you break a 20?
-No, I only have hundreds.

259
00:14:12,685 --> 00:14:14,270
You know what?

260
00:14:14,479 --> 00:14:16,731
I don't always recognize sarcasm,
but I do right now,

261
00:14:16,939 --> 00:14:18,857
and I don't appreciate it.

262
00:14:19,067 --> 00:14:20,526
I'm sorry for your loss.

263
00:14:20,735 --> 00:14:23,571
But you're not the only one
whose day has been a disaster.

264
00:14:30,745 --> 00:14:32,580
That could have killed me.

265
00:14:33,915 --> 00:14:36,584
I can't catch a break.

266
00:14:38,002 --> 00:14:39,045
(INDISTINCT CHATTER ON TV)

267
00:14:39,253 --> 00:14:41,589
I haven't heard from Sheldon
in a while. You think he's okay?

268
00:14:41,798 --> 00:14:43,049
Oh, I'm sure he's fine.

269
00:14:44,175 --> 00:14:45,968
I'm gonna see where he is.

270
00:14:46,177 --> 00:14:47,220
How?

271
00:14:47,428 --> 00:14:49,514
I know his password,
so I can track his phone.

272
00:14:49,722 --> 00:14:51,099
You do that?

273
00:14:51,307 --> 00:14:54,268
Not always, but ever since
he wandered off at the swap meet

274
00:14:54,477 --> 00:14:56,479
chasing a balloon, I get worried.

275
00:14:57,563 --> 00:14:59,065
He can take care of himself.

276
00:14:59,273 --> 00:15:02,901
Look, we went over stranger danger
and gave him that whistle.

277
00:15:03,986 --> 00:15:05,029
That's weird.

278
00:15:05,238 --> 00:15:07,657
-What?
-He's at the train station.

279
00:15:07,865 --> 00:15:09,033
So? He loves trains.

280
00:15:09,242 --> 00:15:12,370
It's dark out and he's alone,
I don't like it. Let's go get him.

281
00:15:12,578 --> 00:15:15,873
Oh, it's sweet how you look out
for him. You're a good guy.

282
00:15:16,082 --> 00:15:19,585
Not just that. My mother would kill
me if I let something happen to him.

283
00:15:24,298 --> 00:15:28,344
-Dude, I'm so sorry.
-Don't take this the wrong way,

284
00:15:28,553 --> 00:15:31,097
but did you do this
for the insurance money?

285
00:15:31,305 --> 00:15:34,475
No. God, you sound
like the police, the firemen,

286
00:15:34,684 --> 00:15:37,395
my parents, my therapist
and the insurance company.

287
00:15:39,063 --> 00:15:41,274
We're here for you, man.
Whatever you need, okay?

288
00:15:41,482 --> 00:15:44,152
Actually, I was wondering if I could
crash at your place for a few nights.

289
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:47,363
Sure, of course. Oh, actually,
Emily was gonna spend the night.

290
00:15:48,239 --> 00:15:50,324
You slept with her? Nice.

291
00:15:50,533 --> 00:15:54,120
Well, I can't take all the credit.
She let me do it to her, but...

292
00:15:57,206 --> 00:15:58,833
But I can always
call her and cancel.

293
00:15:59,041 --> 00:16:01,335
Hang on.
I know a place you can stay,

294
00:16:01,544 --> 00:16:03,504
and earn some money at the same time.

295
00:16:03,713 --> 00:16:05,506
-Great.
-I just have to warn you,

296
00:16:05,715 --> 00:16:09,552
it'll involve humiliation,
degradation and verbal abuse.

297
00:16:10,845 --> 00:16:12,930
So what's the catch?

298
00:16:19,020 --> 00:16:20,104
Sheldon.

299
00:16:20,938 --> 00:16:22,565
You tracked my phone?

300
00:16:22,773 --> 00:16:23,983
Yeah.

301
00:16:24,192 --> 00:16:27,862
Boy, you chase one balloon
for three miles.

302
00:16:30,364 --> 00:16:31,991
We were worried about you.

303
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:34,243
Don't be melodramatic.

304
00:16:34,452 --> 00:16:37,371
I'm just getting on a train
and leaving forever.

305
00:16:38,915 --> 00:16:42,210
Seriously? You don't even have
a change of clothes or a toothbrush.

306
00:16:42,418 --> 00:16:45,213
My plan is to stop
at malls and buy what I need.

307
00:16:45,421 --> 00:16:47,298
It's called living off the land.

308
00:16:48,174 --> 00:16:51,469
Okay, I know you're upset
and there's a lot of stuff going on,

309
00:16:51,677 --> 00:16:54,639
but it's nothing we can't work out.
Come on, let's get you home.

310
00:16:54,847 --> 00:16:58,643
No. I've reached my breaking point.
I need to leave. Now.

311
00:16:58,851 --> 00:17:01,395
-And go where?
-It doesn't matter.

312
00:17:01,604 --> 00:17:04,690
So a few things don't go your way,

313
00:17:04,899 --> 00:17:08,694
and your best decision
is to ride the rails like a hobo?

314
00:17:10,863 --> 00:17:12,490
I suppose it is.

315
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:14,492
Except I have a credit card.

316
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:17,745
And I refuse to carry
my laptop at the end of a stick.

317
00:17:20,831 --> 00:17:23,709
And I'd sooner die
than eat beans out of a can.

318
00:17:25,253 --> 00:17:27,922
Come on, come home with us and
tomorrow I'll take you to Legoland.

319
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:30,800
Legoland is not
the solution to everything.

320
00:17:31,842 --> 00:17:35,179
And it's too much of a scene
since that movie came out.

321
00:17:37,139 --> 00:17:40,518
-Then what can I do?
-Leonard, I am overwhelmed.

322
00:17:41,602 --> 00:17:44,438
Everything is changing
and it's simply too much.

323
00:17:44,647 --> 00:17:46,107
I need to get away and think.

324
00:17:46,315 --> 00:17:49,026
Oh, come on,
you know you're overreacting.

325
00:17:49,235 --> 00:17:52,029
Leonard, hang on.
Just... come here for a second.

326
00:17:54,448 --> 00:17:55,908
Maybe we need to let him go.

327
00:17:56,117 --> 00:17:58,911
-What! Why?
-It might be good for him.

328
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:01,914
You know he can't
take a trip like this by himself.

329
00:18:02,123 --> 00:18:05,209
-He's a grown man.
-No, he looks like a grown man.

330
00:18:07,670 --> 00:18:09,880
You've seen Freaky Friday,
sometimes little kids

331
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:12,091
end up in big person bodies.

332
00:18:13,509 --> 00:18:15,261
Leonard,
we can't protect him forever.

333
00:18:15,469 --> 00:18:18,598
-I know, but--
-He'll be okay.

334
00:18:18,806 --> 00:18:20,391
You taught him well, Padawan.

335
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:25,021
Good Lord! Padawan's the student,
not the teacher.

336
00:18:26,939 --> 00:18:28,608
Seriously, let him go.

337
00:18:35,114 --> 00:18:37,783
Sheldon, if you really need to
do this, I won't stand in your way.

338
00:18:39,035 --> 00:18:40,119
I do.

339
00:18:41,454 --> 00:18:44,290
Okay. Good luck.

340
00:18:48,878 --> 00:18:50,671
Be safe and call us.

341
00:18:53,924 --> 00:18:55,009
I will.

342
00:18:57,386 --> 00:18:58,471
Bye, buddy.

343
00:19:03,768 --> 00:19:06,062
-Sheldon...
-Yes?

344
00:19:07,521 --> 00:19:08,606
I'm gonna miss you.

345
00:19:10,274 --> 00:19:12,150
Of course you are.

346
00:19:14,737 --> 00:19:16,572
He just made that easier.

347
00:19:23,704 --> 00:19:25,122
Hey!

348
00:19:28,167 --> 00:19:31,212
What are you guys still doing here?
I got this, go. Go home.

349
00:19:33,005 --> 00:19:34,799
You sure?

350
00:19:36,092 --> 00:19:38,969
Yeah, she's fed, she took her pills,
she's all tucked in and watching TV.

351
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:41,055
So, she's not too much for you?

352
00:19:41,263 --> 00:19:44,058
Are you kidding?
I love her, she's great.

353
00:19:45,726 --> 00:19:48,187
WOMAN: Stewie, you gonna watch
Wheel of Fortune with me?

354
00:19:48,396 --> 00:19:50,356
Coming, Debbie.

355
00:19:52,358 --> 00:19:55,069
-You call her Debbie?
-She insisted.

356
00:19:55,277 --> 00:19:57,697
So, hey, guys, thank you so much.

357
00:19:57,905 --> 00:19:59,740
This job is a dream come true.

358
00:20:06,497 --> 00:20:08,332
Was that a little weird?

359
00:20:08,541 --> 00:20:09,667
Yeah.

360
00:20:09,875 --> 00:20:13,254
I don't know why,
but something about it feels...

361
00:20:13,462 --> 00:20:15,089
...unnatural.

362
00:20:17,591 --> 00:20:19,260
-Okay, let's go.
-Yep.

363
00:20:21,929 --> 00:20:23,889
Okay, Sheldon,
thanks for checking in.

364
00:20:24,098 --> 00:20:25,975
Talk to you tomorrow?

365
00:20:26,183 --> 00:20:27,685
Okay, bye.

366
00:20:28,769 --> 00:20:30,229
He's okay?

367
00:20:30,438 --> 00:20:32,148
Actually sounds like
he's doing pretty well.

368
00:20:32,356 --> 00:20:34,525
I really think
this is gonna be for the best.

369
00:20:34,734 --> 00:20:38,028
Me too. And he was able
to take a sabbatical from--

370
00:20:38,236 --> 00:20:40,614
How could you let him go!

